{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/9e19c1cd8bca76f1eec39acfa1b09c0f08b67faea5ddce8325e093923d21d394.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x+1},$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-10032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x+1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}-y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-0)-(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{3}{4}|=\\frac{3}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-10032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ccf3768679392a29f79dc096ed286a2df3d27e9c7ef6b0ccde7f6311f4acc9"} {"question" "q-10032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-10032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-10032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $x=16{y}^{4}-1$ and the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{y}^{4}-1 & =0 \\\\ 16{y}^{4} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{16} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/c1e092dd6302bb5948c6452e43b093fc3a531132580c1bb1e42fbe846152f63c.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=16{y}^{4}-1$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ to $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}(16{y}^{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(16{y}^{4}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =32{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y-2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =32\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}|}_{0}^{1/2}-2\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}(\\frac{1}{32}-0)-2(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{4}{5}|=\\frac{4}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78888" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ccf3768679392a29f79dc096ed286a2df3d27e9c7ef6b0ccde7f6311f4acc9"} {"question" "q-78888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78888" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/a45999ec28d309b3be249304e9b5175f66f2b862cd7f18f2c51b3182333e9a08.png)\n\nFind the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =0 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that we want to find the area between the curve $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ccf3768679392a29f79dc096ed286a2df3d27e9c7ef6b0ccde7f6311f4acc9"} {"question" "q-78891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78897" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/cc0f19d50ccd27918d0ac005dec9a8cd27a4f104726ded0d07c71b571ad0522f.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{4-x}$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78897" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{4-x} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4-x \\\\ x & =4-{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1}-{\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(1-0)-(\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78897" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ccf3768679392a29f79dc096ed286a2df3d27e9c7ef6b0ccde7f6311f4acc9"} {"question" "q-78897" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78897" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-78897" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-346783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/assets/816b36f644f3e41d8f48bed2dd49e150d751cb13e082b6a1b9b4ad16973d3d57.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=3\\sqrt{\\frac{x+3}{3}}$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=1$ and $y=2,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-346783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\sqrt{\\frac{x+3}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{x+3}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{x+3}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =x+3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-3)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}\\,|}_{1}^{2}-3\\cdot y\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})-3(2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}-3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So, the area that we want is\n\n$$\nA=|-\\frac{20}{9}|=\\frac{20}{9}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-346783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52ccf3768679392a29f79dc096ed286a2df3d27e9c7ef6b0ccde7f6311f4acc9"} {"question" "q-346783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"} {"question" "q-346783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{20}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059137/state.json" "file_sha256" "98c85c416319975ebb22d06b79815ec8915678423c480b53d4a5829fed52d2a6"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1890 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
